<title>USA: K.C. Council puts $100 mln bond issue on ballot.</title>
<headline>K.C. Council puts $100 mln bond issue on ballot.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-01-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>- The Kansas City, Mo., City Council on Thursday approved putting a $100 million general obligation bond issue on the April ballot.</p>
<p>An aide to Councilman Ed Ford said the measure would be placed on the April 1 ballot.</p>
<p>If approved by voters, proceeds from the bond issue would be used to buy out Kansas City Power and Light Company's share of the city's streetlighting system and allow the city to upgrade the system by adding up to three times as many streetlights.</p>
<p>((--Karen Pierog, 312-408-8647))</p>
